Introduction to Mathematics: Math is the study of numbers, shapes, and patterns.
Number System: Addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.
Fractions and Decimals: Understanding parts of a whole.
Geometry: Shapes, lines, and angles.
Measurement: Length, weight, capacity, and time.
Data Handling: Collecting and organizing information.
Patterns and Symmetry: Recognizing repetitions and balance.
Money: Understanding currency and basic transactions.
Problem Solving: Applying math to real-life situations.
Mental Math: Quick calculations and logical thinking.
